\description{
Layers are \code{torch} modules built on \code{\link[=message_passing]{message_passing()}}. Every layer takes
node features \code{x} (an N by F tensor, or \code{list(x_src, x_dst)} for bipartite
relations where noted) and a one based long \code{edge_index} (2 by E, row 1
source, row 2 target), and returns one row per target node. Messages flow
from source to target, so a node aggregates over its \strong{incoming} edges.
For undirected graphs, \code{\link[=graph_data]{graph_data()}} stores both directions, so this is
the usual neighborhood.
}
