Cost is \eqn{O(E F)} for message construction plus the dense transforms
(\eqn{O(N F F')}); attention layers keep an E by heads attention tensor;
\code{nn_conv} stores an E by F by F' tensor of edge specific weights and is the
most memory hungry. All layers are permutation equivariant: permuting node
rows and relabeling \code{edge_index} permutes the output rows the same way.

The formulas follow the PyTorch Geometric layers of the same names
(\code{SAGEConv}, \code{GCNConv}, \code{GraphConv}, \code{GINConv}/\code{GINEConv}, \code{GATConv},
\code{GATv2Conv}, \code{TransformerConv}, \code{NNConv}, \code{RGCNConv}) for the options
exposed here; options not listed are not implemented.

Attention layers keep the coefficients of their last forward pass
in \code{layer$last_attention} (a list with \code{edge_index} and an E by heads
tensor \code{alpha}). Attention coefficients describe how the model weighted
neighbors; they are not by themselves measures of feature importance or
causal relevance.
}
